# Interactive HTML Widgets
### Embedded Controls for Live Demonstrations

Slides can include real interactive UI widgets that respond to presenter clicks:

<div class="my-8 p-8 rounded-3xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 flex items-center justify-between max-w-3xl mx-auto shadow-2xl">
  <div>
    <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Live Click Counter</h3>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-300">Click the button below to test live slide script execution.</p>
  </div>
  <button id="demoClickBtn" class="px-8 py-4 rounded-2xl font-bold text-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-indigo-600 hover:from-blue-600 hover:to-indigo-700 text-white shadow-xl shadow-indigo-500/30 active:scale-95 transition-all cursor-pointer">
    Clicks: <span id="clickCount">0</span>
  </button>
</div>

<script>
  let count = 0;
  const btn = document.getElementById('demoClickBtn');
  const label = document.getElementById('clickCount');
  if (btn && label) {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      count++;
      label.textContent = count;
      btn.style.transform = 'scale(0.95)';
      setTimeout(() => { btn.style.transform = 'scale(1)'; }, 100);
    });
  }
</script>

- Safely executed in a scoped container context
- Event listeners are automatically detached upon leaving the slide

